  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing self-awareness about humor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the top text overlay 'i know you shouldn't laugh at 9/11 jokes', which uses the second-person pronoun 'you' to address the viewer directly. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the recipient of the moral statement, implying they are the one who 'shouldn't laugh' but is being invited to laugh anyway. The projection is onto the textual material, which frames the user as the subject of the moral injunction.",
